---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';

export const prerender = true;

const domain = SITE.email.split('@')[1];
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} collects, uses and protects your information.`}
  lede="What we collect, why we collect it, and how to tell us to stop."
  updated="October 2, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains how {SITE.name} ("we", "us") handles information when you visit
    <strong>{SITE.url}</strong>. We have tried to write it in plain language. If anything is
    unclear, email <a href={`mailto:privacy@${domain}`}>privacy@{domain}</a> and we will explain.
  </p>

  <h2>Information and browser storage</h2>
  <p>There is no account system or login on this site.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Messages you send.</strong> If you email us directly, we receive your email address
      and the information in your message. The contact form currently shown on the site is a demo
      and does not send or store submissions.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Saved ideas and reading preferences.</strong> The save buttons and text-size control
      store post IDs and your selected text size in your browser's local storage. This information
      stays in that browser and is not sent to us. You can clear it through your browser settings.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical request data.</strong> Our hosting provider may process information such as
      your IP address, browser, and requested page to deliver and protect the site. The provider's
      own retention and security practices also apply.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Third-party technologies.</strong> If advertising is enabled, Google and its partners
      may use cookies or similar technologies as described below. The site also loads Pinterest's
      sharing script; Pinterest may process information under its own privacy policy.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>The site does not currently offer an email newsletter signup or collect payment details.</p>
<h2>How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To operate, maintain, and protect the site.</li>
    <li>To reply to messages you send us directly.</li>
    <li>To display advertising if Google AdSense is enabled for the site.</li>
  </ul>
<h2>Advertising and Google AdSense</h2>
  <p>
    If Google AdSense is enabled on this site, Google and its advertising partners may use cookies,
    web beacons, IP addresses, or similar identifiers to serve, measure, and personalize ads. These
    technologies may use information about your visits to this and other sites. Google explains
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">how it uses data on partner sites</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can opt out of personalised advertising by visiting
    <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>,
    or opt out of third-party vendor cookies at
    <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">aboutads.info</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Consent in the EEA, UK and Switzerland</h2>
  <p>
    Where consent is required, Google AdSense is enabled only after a Google-certified Consent
    Management Platform has been configured to collect and respect your choices. When active, the
    message and available settings depend on your location. If you have a question about a consent
    message, contact <a href={`mailto:privacy@${domain}`}>privacy@{domain}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We do not sell your personal information. Information may be processed by:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google</strong> — advertising delivery and measurement, if AdSense is enabled.</li>
    <li><strong>Our hosting provider</strong> — to serve and protect the site.</li>
    <li><strong>Pinterest</strong> — when its sharing script is loaded or you use a Pinterest link.</li>
    <li><strong>Legal authorities</strong> — where we are legally required to.</li>
  </ul>
<h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, export or delete the
    personal information we hold about you, and to object to certain processing. Residents of the
    EEA and UK have these rights under the GDPR; California residents have comparable rights under
    the CCPA/CPRA, including the right not to be discriminated against for exercising them.
  </p>
  <p>
    To make a request, email <a href={`mailto:privacy@${domain}`}>privacy@{domain}</a>. We will
    respond within 30 days.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention and security</h2>
  <p>
    We retain direct email messages for as long as needed to handle the conversation and meet our
    legal obligations. Saved ideas and reading preferences remain in your browser until you clear
    its local storage. The site is served over HTTPS. No method of transmission over the internet
    is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
  </p>
<h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We will update this page when our practices change, and we will move the "last updated" date at
    the top. Material changes will be noted on the homepage.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:privacy@${domain}`}>privacy@{domain}</a>.
  </p>

  <hr />
  <p>
    <em>
      This template is a starting point, not legal advice. Have a solicitor or attorney review it
      against your jurisdiction and your actual data practices before you launch.
    </em>
  </p>
</PageLayout>
